Feel the jungle beat

2
00:06:51,428 --> 00:06:57,428
The Jungle Book 2 is a family, animation, adventure
film directed by Steve Trenbirth.

3
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:23,142
Mowgli has been living in the man-village with his little
stepbrother Ranjan and his best friend Shanti.

4
00:13:42,857 --> 00:13:48,857
But the man-cub still has that jungle rhythm in his heart, and
he misses his old buddies Baloo and Bagheera.

5
00:17:08,571 --> 00:17:14,571
When Mowgli wanders back to the wild for some swingin' fun, he soon finds the
man-eating tiger Shere Khan is lurking in the shadows and planning his revenge.

6
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
Mowgli (voice), played by Haley Joel Osment.

7
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Baloo (voice), played by John Goodman.

8
00:27:25,714 --> 00:27:31,714
Shanti (voice), played by Mae Whitman.

9
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Ranjan (voice), played by Connor Funk.

10
00:34:17,142 --> 00:34:23,142
Bagheera (voice), played by Bob Joles.

11
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Shere Khan (voice), played by Tony Jay.

12
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
The Jungle Book 2 is a 2003 animated adventure film produced by the Australian office at
DisneyToon Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures and Buena Vista Distribution.

13
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
The film was released in France on February 5, 2003, and
released in the United States on February 14.

14
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The film is a sequel to Walt Disney's 1967 film The Jungle Book, and stars Haley Joel
Osment as the voice of Mowgli and John Goodman as the voice of Baloo.

15
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
The film was originally produced as a direct-to-video film, but was released
theatrically first, similar to the Peter Pan sequel Return to Never Land.

16
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
It is the fourth animated Disney sequel to have a theatrical release rather than going direct-to-video after The Rescuers Down Under
(1990), Fantasia 2000 (1999), and Return to Never Land (2002) and the last one until Ralph Breaks the Internet (2018).

17
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
The film is not based on The Second Jungle Book, but
they do have several characters in common.

18
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
The film received negative reviews criticizing the animation and plot, but it was a box
office success, grossing $135.7 million against a $20 million budget.

19
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
The film explores themes of tiger, river, village, cartoon, musical.

20
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
The tone is lighthearted.
